    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d498">

                <pb facs="0949" n="825" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg825"/>

                <head>No. 494.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Señor de
                        Zamacona.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-02-19"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 19,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I had the honor to receive upon the 15th
                    instant the note of Mr. Navarro, the chargé d’affaires <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ad interim</hi> of Mexico, bearing date the 10th of the present month, in
                    which, by direction of his government, he has informed me that it is the desire
                    of Mexico that the treaty between it and the United States of July 10, 1868,
                    concerning naturalization and citizenship, shall be terminated at the expiration
                    of the twelve months, as provided for in article 5 of such convention.</p>
                <p>Observing that due note has been taken of this announcement, I take the present
                    occasion to offer, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
